    "dek": "Boxing training is one of the best ways to get a great workout while having fun.",
    "body": "<p>Boxing training is one of the best ways to get a great workout while having fun. At Fighters Boxing Gym, we teach real boxing skills as you burn calories and get fit. Fitness boxers, aka non-contact boxers, just need to remember a few important things to maximize the workout while maximizing fun.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Immerse yourself.</strong> Take the opportunity to leave your troubles behind for an hour. Enjoy a reprieve from the stressors of your day.</li>\n<li><strong>Try new things.</strong> A new combo. A new piece of equipment. Expand your toolbox and access something new to keep boxing fun.</li>\n<li><strong>Switch stances.</strong> Right-handed? Try a few rounds in the southpaw stance. You can speed up skill-building by training about 5%-50% of any given workout in the opposite stance.</li>\n<li><strong>Protect your hands.</strong> Use proper hand wraps and gloves. Punch correctly. Gradually increase impact. Take care of your hands so they can take care of you.</li>\n<li><strong>Ask questions.</strong> Our coaches are in the gym to help you, but none of us are mind-readers. We love to talk boxing. Tell us your goal(s) so our coaches can get you going in the right direction.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Come by Fighters Nashville to discuss your goals with an authentic boxing coach who’s trained to help.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Founder and Director of Fighters, Dr. Christy Halbert has used her background as an academic in sociology, collegiate athlete, and professional boxer to take a multi-disciplinary approach to the sport of boxing. Halbert was a 2012 Olympic Coach for Team USA, and is a IWBHF Inductee.</p>\n</blockquote>"
